Papiverse — Project Modules
Papiverse is a secure operations and financial management platform built for Krispy Papi. For a portfolio, the system can be presented through these key modules:
1. Authentication and Access Control
Secure user login and session management
Role-based permissions and protected routes
User account and credential management
Unauthorized-access handling
2. Branch Management
Internal and external branch records
Branch addresses, delivery fees, and operational details
Purchase-order monitoring
Branch payment reports
Branch profitability rankings
3. Inventory Management
Supply and raw-material inventory
Stock level monitoring
Inventory adjustments and movement history
Branch-level inventory visibility
4. Supply Order Management
Supply-order creation and processing
Multi-stage approval workflow
Order status and payment tracking
Detailed purchase-order reports
5. Product Catalog
Centralized supply catalog
Raw-material management
Product pricing and availability records
Reusable product data across inventory and orders
6. Finance and Expense Management
Business expense recording
Finance account monitoring
Supply and raw-material cost breakdowns
Meat purchase-order management
Financial data organized by responsible account or owner
7. Reports and Analytics
Weekly sales reports
Commission reports
Settlement reports
Supply and raw-material reports
Branch profit rankings and performance comparisons
8. Payment and Settlement Tracking
Branch payment monitoring
Supply-order payment records
Settlement history
Outstanding-balance tracking
9. Audit Logs
Supply and raw-material activity logs
Inventory input and order histories
Transaction-level audit trails
Improved accountability and traceability
10. Administration
User management
Roles and authority configuration
Permission-based navigation
Administrative control over system access
11. Account Management
Personal and branch information
Profile editing
Credential updates
Account details and assigned responsibilities
12. Real-Time Notifications
Live operational updates
Order and approval notifications
WebSocket-based event delivery
User feedback through alerts and status messages
Technology Stack
Next.js 16 and React 19
TypeScript
Tailwind CSS and shadcn/ui
TanStack Query for server-state management
STOMP, SockJS, and WebSockets for real-time updates
Recharts for data visualization
REST API integration
Responsive, role-based user interface